---
description: >
  Brevity-sweep audit of `src/tools/upgrade/buildVersionsMeta/.aide` — small spec (25 lines) close to all caps, but `outcomes.desired[0]` enumerates the artifact category set verbatim.
intent: >
  buildVersionsMeta is a build-time script generating versions.json. Spec
  is structurally fine but `outcomes.desired[0]` carries an exact-list
  enumeration of artifact categories (methodology docs, commands, agents,
  skills, extensions) — forbidden content.
misalignment:
  - spec-bloat
---

## Issues

- [ ] `description` is 165 chars (under cap, fine).

- [ ] `intent` is 77 words (under cap, fine).

- [ ] `outcomes.desired` has 4 items (at cap, fine on count). Item 0
  enumerates "methodology docs, commands, agents, skills, and extensions"
  — exact category list. Forbidden content; the contract should commit
  to "every deliverable artifact is covered" without naming the categories.
  Traces to: `outcomes.desired[0]` | Forbidden content (CLI/category enumeration)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Forbidden-content

- [ ] `outcomes.undesired` has 4 items (at cap, fine on count). Item 1
  reproduces the same category list ("docs only," etc.) — same forbidden
  enumeration in negative form.
  Traces to: `outcomes.undesired[1]` | Forbidden content
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Forbidden-content

- [ ] No body sections at all (no `## Context`, `## Strategy`, `## Good
  examples`, `## Bad examples`, `## References`). Required by the contract.
  Traces to: body section completeness | spec-gap (missing required body sections)
  Misalignment: spec-gap
  Category: structural-gap

- [ ] Carry-forward (prior cycle): 2 unchecked items (extensions category
  silently absent because the .vsix has no git history) — real
  implementation issue that survives the brevity rewrite.

## Retro

This spec is structurally minimal but trips the forbidden-content scan
on category enumeration in both desired and undesired. The fix is
"every deliverable artifact category in the canonical content registry
appears in versions.json with version metadata"; the canonical registry
is the source of truth, so listing the categories in the spec is
duplication that goes stale.
